  "quote_spans": [
    {
      "chunk_id": 200,
      "char_start": 476,
      "char_end": 814,
      "text": "As she was\nstanding one day with Gjert on the quay, about to start for home, Fru\nBeck passed a little way off, leaning on her husband's arm, and looked\nback with an expression so sad, and with eyes that seemed to linger so\nlongingly, as if she had something she wanted to say, or to confide,\nthat they nodded involuntarily to one another"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 202,
      "char_start": 268,
      "char_end": 917,
      "text": "Old Beck's grandson, Frederick, who was going to be a naval cadet, had\nfancied one day that he would escape observation from the windows at\nhome by climbing up to join his friend at the mast-head, on the other\nside of the mast; but the slender spar was not sufficient to protect him\nfrom the master-pilot's keen eye, and the latter came himself on board\nin full grandfatherly indignation against the skipper for allowing such\npranks to be played on board his craft, thrashed Gjert for being the\ncause of his grandson's disobedience, and told him that it was very\nclear what he would come to some day--that he came of a bad stock, and\ntook after it"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 203,
      "char_start": 532,
      "char_end": 924,
      "text": "Henrik, however, had\nentirely forgotten her injunctions in the more interesting occupation of\ncatching shrimps in one of the salt-water pools which a recent high tide\nhad left among the rocks; and there, in the bright afternoon, over the\nblue and gold sea, dotted with sails, was the boat with its stripe and\nnumber already close by, standing straight in for the harbour with a\nflowing sheet"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 204,
      "char_start": 1497,
      "char_end": 1761,
      "text": "When Gjert was in the boat, Elizabeth had a sort of security\nthat Salve would at all events not be absolutely reckless; and Gjert\nalways took care that she should have news of them by other pilots or\nfishermen from Merdoe, from the different places they put in to"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 205,
      "char_start": 1259,
      "char_end": 1542,
      "text": "His mother could not, however, so easily dismiss the ambitious scheme\nfrom her mind, and it became, a few days after, the occasion of the most\nviolent scene which had ever yet put her strength of purpose to the\ntest, but from which there ensued eventually the very happiest results"
    }
  ],
